          "text": "Jacob’s Well — JACOB’S WELL: The well is about 100 feet (30.5 meters) in depth and one yard (.9 meter) in diameter, cut through limestone. Fed by subterranean streams from the adjacent mountain slopes, the water is pure and plentiful, the pride of the villagers. A church has existed on the site from at least AD 380. The Greek Orthodox Church acquired the site in 1885 and built a structure on the site. Access to the well is by steps leading from either side of the church altar to the well curb below. (Source: Aquifer Open Bible Dictionary, CC-BY-SA-4.0)",
          "evidence_id": "EV-DICT-0002",
